# Server declarations

**Status:** current. `@on` and trailing `json` are **removed**.

Bodies are Roc, not templates. Module-level only.

| Declaration | Default method | Success | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `@context { … }` | — | `State` type | One per module |
| `@init { … }` | — | context value | `?` → process exit |
| `@view("path")` | GET | HTML document | Always GET |
| `@patch("path")` | POST | Fragment → patch-elements | GET rejected; `:put` `:patch` `:delete` allowed |
| `@command("path")` | POST | Roc data → empty SSE or JSON | GET rejected |
| `@live` | generated GET `/sse` | Fragment stream | One per module |

Dispatch calls `handler!(context, request)`. Write `|{ db }, request|` when
you read the request. One-parameter lists append `_request`. Omit params for
`|state, _request|`.

`@patch:post` is rejected (POST is already the default). `@patch:patch` is
legal. `@view("/sse")` plus `@live` is a diagnostic.

Complete matrix: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

**Related:** [Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/).
